.TH TIMELINE 6
.SH NAME
timeline \- lanes and spans of time, for rtrace
.SH DESCRIPTION
A timeline is text, a record to a line, that
.IR rtrace (1)
draws.
It holds
.IR lanes ,
rows that may nest under one another,
and
.IR spans ,
intervals of time on a lane,
each of a
.IR kind
that gives its color.
.PP
The first line is the magic and the version:
.IP
.EX
timeline 1
.EE
.PP
Each line after it is a record: a name, then fields separated by blanks
(spaces or tabs).
The last field of a record is the rest of its line, blanks and all.
A blank line, and a line that starts with
.LR # ,
holds nothing.
A reader skips a record whose name it does not know,
so a later version may add records that this one's readers pass over;
one that changes what a record here means changes the version.
.TP
.BI kind " id name"
The display name of a kind.
.I Id
is a word, the one spans name;
.I name
is the rest of the line.
Kinds take colors in the order of their
.B kind
records, and a kind that has none takes the next color when a span first names it.
.TP
.BI lane " id parent start end label"
A lane.
.I Id
is a word, unique among lanes.
.I Parent
is the
.I id
of the lane it nests under, or
.L -
for none; a parent may come after its children.
.I Start
and
.I end
are its life, in nanoseconds, or
.L -
when the lane's own spans give it.
.I Label
is the rest of the line.
.TP
.BI span " lane start end kind name detail"
A span on lane
.IR lane ,
from
.I start
to
.IR end ,
in nanoseconds, with
.I start
no later than
.IR end .
.I Kind
is a kind's
.IR id ;
.I name
is a word that groups spans, a system call's name for one, which
.IR rtrace 's
table counts;
.I detail
is the rest of the line, what
.I rtrace
shows for the span.
A span may name a lane that has no
.B lane
record; the lane is then its own label, with no parent.
.PP
Times are decimal integers, nanoseconds from any origin the writer chooses,
the same for every line; a reader shows them from the earliest.
Records may come in any order.
.SH EXAMPLES
A shell that forks a child, which runs
.IR echo (1):
.IP
.EX
timeline 1
kind io files and I/O
kind proc processes
lane 35 - - - 35 rc
lane 37 35 - - 37 rc → echo
span 35 1000 4200 io open Open "/env/home" 0x0 = 4
span 35 5000 5100 proc rfork Rfork 0x2014 = 37
span 37 6000 6400 io pwrite Pwrite 1 "hi." 3 -1 = 3
span 35 5200 9000 proc await Await = 23
.EE
.SH "SEE ALSO"
.IR ratrace (1),
.IR rtrace (1)
